      "source_bound": true,
      "source_id": "SRCV2_a9c5e690432dea7e",
      "source_span": "page:11;section:51. DESeq2 was used to normalize by size factor (reads per sample);paragraph:31-33",
      "sparse_rank": 1,
      "text": "as well as by library complexity, and we then applied Wald test to determine significance of differential expression. Public gene expression data. ImmGen raw expression data of phases 1 and 2 were downloaded as CEL files from the Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO; GSE15907 and GSE37448), processed, and normalized using the robust multi- array average procedure on probe-level data using Matlab functions. The analysis was performed using a custom CDF file obtained from Brainarray and Encode data were processed as we described previously53. Raw counts from the lung reference data set were obtained from Gibbings et al.29 (GSE94135) and Altboum et al.28 (GSE49932). Counts were normalized and converted to TPM using R functions. The gene expression profile of GM-CSF-derived bone marrow dendritic cell subsets (available at GSE6236119) was analyzed using the GEO2R tool for differentially expressed...",
      "title": "Reference-based analysis of lung single-cell sequencing reveals a transitional profibrotic macrophage",
      "tool_name": "SingleR",
      "tool_names": [
        "SingleR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "canonical_task": "cell_type_annotation",
      "chunk_id": "uat-authoritative-span:singler.interface",
